&lt;p&gt;As a member of the Technical Program Management Team team you will own cloud capacity programs work from idea to production. You will pair with colleagues in research and product and be trusted with real responsibility early.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Build evaluation harnesses that track quality, latency and cost release over release.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Design, build and operate cloud capacity programs services that run in production.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Debug failures end to end, from data pipelines to model behaviour.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Keep dashboards and runbooks for cloud capacity programs accurate and easy to follow.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;A record of owning a system from the first commit to steady operation.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with program tooling.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Clear written communication and a preference for simple designs.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Comfort reading research papers and turning them into working code.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Experience with distributed training or large-scale data processing.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Prior work on evaluation, red-teaming or reliability for learned systems.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
